           TLSF corpus (1,586 files)

host:      11th Gen Core i7-11850H, 8 cores / 16 threads, 15 GB, zram swap ~7 GB in use.
           Little headroom above the 8 GiB cap: trust MEMOUT rows less than timeouts.

panel-census/   22 arms (arms.list), each alone, over
                tests/suites/benchmarks/syntcomp26/panel.list (180 instances).
                Staged caps 1,5,17; read at cap <= 17 through smallest_cap_solved.
                8 GiB MemoryMax, zero swap, one invocation at a time, no CPU limit.
                2026-09-10 13:07 to 2026-09-11 01:32.

hard-set/       10 arms (arms.list), each alone, over instances.list: the 353 of 1,524
                that otf_sparse_formula leaves undecided in the closing threeway campaign,
                _bm-logs.spot-otf-20260907/full-closing/otf_sparse_formula-summary.tsv
                (1,171 decided at a uniform 17 s).
                Uniform 17 s cap, 8 GiB, zero swap, one invocation at a time, no CPU limit.
                2026-09-11 01:33 to 19:12. Arm 4 (unreal:formula:backward) was interrupted
                by a session restart after 22 instances and resumed with --resume; rows are
                fsynced per instance, so the one in flight was simply re-run.

race-curve/     One race invocation per instance per config (configs.list) over
                instances.list: the panel plus the hard set, 494 after an overlap of 39.
                Uniform 17 s, 8 GiB for the whole race, zero swap, CPUQuota=400%.
                AllowedCPUs was tried first and is silently ignored here, because the user
                manager is not delegated cpuset; that attempt ran a few minutes unpinned and
                is kept as _bm-logs.20260911-race-curve-UNPINNED-partial, not evidence.
                Summaries are added here when the run completes.

not here:  the raw per-run TSVs, which stay in the gitignored _bm-logs.20260910-arm-census,
